    "author": "Fasal Kavach team",
    "why": "No real farmer registry was available, and using one without consent would be wrong. These 12 farms are invented. Village names, coordinates and agronomic windows are real; the farms and their owners are not.",
    "design": "Sowing dates are chosen so that, in August 2026, the twelve farms sit in ten different growth stages across the four grid cells. That exercises every branch of the crop calendar and the stage-sensitivity rules in one ingest run.",
    "not_synthetic": "Weather is NOT synthetic. Every rainfall and temperature figure the rules act on is fetched live from Open-Meteo at ingest time. The farms are made up; the climate signal is real.",
    "no_wheat_note": "August is kharif season in Jharkhand. Wheat is a rabi crop sown in November-December, so seeding a wheat farm with a July sowing date would be agronomically wrong. Wheat and frost rules are covered by the test suite instead of the seed data."
  },
